- `node --check server.js`: passed.
- `node --check lib/agent-discovery.js`: passed.
- `node --check test/agent-discovery.test.js`: passed.
- `git diff --check`: passed.
- `node --test test/agent-discovery.test.js`: passed.
- All non-socket suites: 15/15 file suites passed, including the discovery
  endpoint + caller matrix suite.
- `npm test`: 15/18 file suites passed. The only failures were these pre-existing
  socket-bound suites, rejected before assertions by loopback `listen()` EPERM:
  - `test/access-control.test.js`
  - `test/managed-repos.test.js`
  - `test/publish.test.js`
- `node scripts/validate-raw-html.js; echo $?`: exit 1.
- `node scripts/validate-editable-mode.js; echo $?`: exit 1.
- Socket-bound validators:
  - `scripts/validate-raw-html.js`
  - `scripts/validate-editable-mode.js`

Both validators fail before assertions because this execution sandbox rejects
`listen(0, '127.0.0.1')` with `EPERM: operation not permitted`. Their required
exit-0 result cannot be truthfully recorded here and must be rerun in an
environment that permits loopback socket binding.
